{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIwL0xhZHklMjBPZiUyMEd1YWRhbHVwZSUyMCUyODIwMjAlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Lady Of Guadalupe","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/itIjhwzELVcfIIrSKuon9iKtdFY.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cTL00gmV029FgE5Q8f1bvcsdHzF.jpg","description":"Based on true events, \"Lady of Guadalupe\" is a moving religious discovery juxtaposing folklore and the present day. Historically significant recreations are used to illustrate the origin of her prevalent and powerful symbolism of Mexican identity and faith. When a young and ambitious reporter (Guillermo Iván) is assigned an article on faith, he finds himself enmeshed in the legend of Juan Diego and Our Lady of Guadalupe. Skeptical of miracles and the importance of modern-day Christianity, the reporter's investigation takes him from cynic to true believer as his personal limits are tested.","releaseInfo":"2020","genres":["Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.4","runtime":"95 min","cast":["Guillermo Iván","Jesús Lloveras","Kimberley Peterson","Paola Baldion","Christopher Phipps","Eric da Silva","Hash Patel","Gary J. Neuger"],"director":["Pedro Brenner"],"released":"2020-11-30T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Guillermo Iván","character":"John Martinez / Juan Diego","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/zH8BOepVqv3l1uQvHfRyPSX65OJ.jpg"},{"name":"Jesús Lloveras","character":"Spaniard Juan","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/c4qASKR8pxBxSYwLWd937VzkdRw.jpg"},{"name":"Kimberley Peterson","character":"Mary","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/xFkQQ5AHTFjpvvNb1HlBOKKVTO2.jpg"},{"name":"Paola Baldion","character":"Lady of Guadalupe"},{"name":"Christopher Phipps","character":"Professor Collins"},{"name":"Eric da Silva","character":"Father Da Gand","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/c7VoexEHz40xNkKxiYOpIa9GH05.jpg"},{"name":"Hash Patel","character":"Dr. Patel","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/peZ